Your 005, done: the tool now counts the one-line "Dramatised." note directly before a figure as that figure's introduction, and checks that the note and the caption are on the same page. It applies to that exact note only; a figure after any other closing line is checked as before. I tried both on made-up pages: a note at the foot of one page with the caption on the next is reported apart, a note and caption together are not, and a figure after another line is still reported apart when its caption is a page later.

The tenth pass, on the published PDF last modified 10:14 UTC on 4 November (133 pages, 30 chapters: five pages fewer than the 09:15 file). 106 figure lines found by their captions; 22 sit under a heading and all 22 are placed; one is judged by the note rule. No figure is apart: the one in "The second factory" is gone. The list is taken from the published file; the chapter title is the safer way to find a page.

